2026-10-07 Florian Pein, version 1.3-0

  * examples with \donttest{} code take a few minutes at most instead of up to
    twenty, requested by CRAN: Monte-Carlo simulations in the examples use
    fewer repetitions, r = 1e3 for jsmurf, jules and stepDetection and r = 100
    for the refinement step of hilde and improveSmallScales

  * HILDE allowing heterogeneous noise is only illustrated in hilde.Rd, with
    a given critical value q2 for the lengths 3, 10 and 25, its Monte-Carlo
    simulation takes about an hour

  * the examples of jules and hilde define the time points before zooming
    into a single event, before they plotted the function stats::time

2026-09-30 Florian Pein, version 1.3-0

  * removed the vignette, the package no longer suggests R.rsp and has no
    vignette builder

  * the documentation refers to Pein, Eltzner, Munk (2021),
    <doi:10.1007/s00249-021-01506-8>, instead of the vignette; added the paper
    to the references in jsmurf.Rd, jules.Rd, hilde.Rd, improveSmallScales.Rd
    and getCritVal.Rd

2026-09-12 Florian Pein, version 1.3-0

  * the vignette is now the authors' version of Pein, Eltzner, Munk (2021),
    <doi:10.1007/s00249-021-01506-8>, typeset from our own sources

  * it is shipped as a prebuilt PDF ('asis' vignette); the raster panels
    of the plots are stored with an 8 bit palette instead of 24 bit colour

  * inst/CITATION now cites the paper and no longer reports the year as '????'

  * given and family name of the maintainer were the wrong way round in the
    DESCRIPTION file, which made the package show up as by 'Pein Florian'

  * added the paper to the references in clampSeg-package.Rd and replaced
    references to numbered vignette sections by their names

  * updated the description in the DESCRIPTION file

2026-09-07 Florian Pein, version 1.2-1

  * Monte-Carlo simulations in the tests and in the examples are now cached in the
    session's temporary directory instead of the user's cache directory,
    fixes the CRAN note about new files in '~/.cache/R/R.cache/stepR'

  * new test file test_cacheLocation.R, ensures that no simulation is cached
    outside of the temporary directory

